# Always

## No shortcuts

- NEVER weaken ESLint/Biome/Clippy/Ruff/basedpyright/hooks or edit `tsconfig*` /
  `pyproject.toml` tool tables to dodge errors (unless the user explicitly asks).
  NEVER `--no-verify`.
- NEVER add `eslint-disable*` / `biome-ignore` / `@ts-ignore` /
  `@ts-expect-error` / `@ts-nocheck` / `#[allow(clippy::…)]` / `# type: ignore` /
  `# noqa` without user **yes**. Fix the code, or follow `800-lint-suppression-beg`.
- NEVER paper over races or errors (empty catch, sentinel null/false, sleep,
  fire-and-forget). See `800-no-lazy`.
- JS/TS: NEVER vanilla Promise/async/throw/Zod where Effect and Schema apply.
  See `800-effect` and `100-strong-types`.
- Python: ALWAYS `uv`. See `020-python`.
- ALWAYS complete work 100% or stop and ask.

## Validate

- After mid-feature edits: run the root `validate` script. Read **all**
  failures; fix every diagnostic; one confirm.
- NEVER skip the gate; NEVER stop at first error.

## Tests and docs first

- ALWAYS update the docs wiki and write the failing test before production code
  when adding a feature or changing behavior. See `050-docs`.
- NEVER implement behavior first and retrofit tests or docs afterward.
